  "name": "snarky",
  "description": "An OCaml front-end DSL for constructing Rank-1 Constraint Systems (R1CS) used in zk-SNARKs. It employs a monadic interface to facilitate the development of provable computations, allowing developers to write high-level functional code that compiles into arithmetic circuits. The toolkit provides modular cryptographic primitives, including elliptic curve operations, sponge-based hash functions, and Merkle tree verification.",
